  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed outbuilding, by reason of its&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;design and excessive height, would present a discordant feature which is at odds with the character and appearance of the surrounding area,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;notably given the location of the application site within the Becontree Estate.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposed development is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework &amp;nbsp;(NPPF) (December 2024) - Polies D1, D4, D5, D6 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) -&amp;nbsp; Policies&amp;nbsp; DMD1, DMD4, DMD5,&amp;nbsp; SP2 and SPP6 of&amp;nbsp; the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024) - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed outbuilding, be reason of its excessive height, would result in unacceptable loss of daylight, overshadowing and overbearing impacts impacts to neighbouring properties&amp;nbsp; no.167 and 171 Lichfield Road.&amp;nbsp; Therefore, the proposal would constitute unneighbourly development which is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024); - Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); - Policies DMD1, DMD5 and DMSI3 of&amp;nbsp; The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024); and - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
